    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `audit:` step of the owner-creation pipeline (`AuditOwnerCreated`, wired in `owners.POST.yml`) already emitted a human-readable audit line on the `AUDIT` logger. I added an immutable structured event alongside it.\n\n**New file \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** (immutable `record`):\n- Components declared in spec order, which is also the JSON field order: `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event}`.\n- A `from(int seq, Owner owner)` factory sources `customerCode` from `owner.getCustomerCode()`. This is the single point that supplies the event's **primary identifier** \u2014 so when the customerCode is later unified into the memberId (i.e. `getCustomerCode()` yields the memberId), the event carries it with no change here, exactly as the spec requires.\n- `event` is fixed to `OWNER_CREATED`.\n\n**`AuditOwnerCreated.java`**:\n- Kept the existing audit line unchanged.\n- Added a static `AtomicInteger` sequence (monotonically increasing across all creates) and a static Jackson 3 `JsonMapper`.\n- Emits the event as JSON on the `AUDIT` logger: e.g. `{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.\n\nThe sequence counter and mapper are `static` because OfficeFloor may instantiate the function per request, so `seq` must be shared to stay monotonic across creates.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` and the full suite pass (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`).",
